code\u003e [10]\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003estring\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eThe \u003ca href=\"https://agentskills.io/specification#skill-md-format\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003edescription of the Agent Skill\u003c/a\u003e. [11]\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003eReview a changelist against the team's review policy.\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca href=\"/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions-genai/blob/main/docs/registry/attributes/gen-ai.md\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003egen_ai.skill.source.uri\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/51c52913babf0af7e3699435eb2fa53f65cf91d89c23a9e0edba0fdd9de155d0/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f2d646576656c6f706d656e742d626c7565\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/51c52913babf0af7e3699435eb2fa53f65cf91d89c23a9e0edba0fdd9de155d0/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f2d646576656c6f706d656e742d626c7565\" alt=\"Development\" data-canonical-src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/-development-blue\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003eRecommended\u003c/code\u003e [12]\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003estring\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eThe source URI for loading the skill. [13]\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003ehttps://skills.example.com/code-review\u003c/code\u003e; \u003ccode\u003egs://example-skills/code-review\u003c/code\u003e; \u003ccode\u003efile:///opt/skills/code-review\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca href=\"/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions-genai/blob/main/docs/registry/attributes/gen-ai.md\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003egen_ai.tool.description\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/51c52913babf0af7e3699435eb2fa53f65cf91d89c23a9e0edba0fdd9de155d0/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f2d646576656c6f706d656e742d626c7565\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/51c52913babf0af7e3699435eb2fa53f65cf91d89c23a9e0edba0fdd9de155d0/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f2d646576656c6f706d656e742d626c7565\" alt=\"Development\" data-canonical-src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/-development-blue\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003eRecommended\u003c/code\u003e If available.\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003estring\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eThe tool description. [14]\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003eMultiply two numbers\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca href=\"/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions-genai/blob/main/docs/registry/attributes/gen-ai.md\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003egen_ai.tool.type\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/51c52913babf0af7e3699435eb2fa53f65cf91d89c23a9e0edba0fdd9de155d0/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f2d646576656c6f706d656e742d626c7565\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/51c52913babf0af7e3699435eb2fa53f65cf91d89c23a9e0edba0fdd9de155d0/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f2d646576656c6f706d656e742d626c7565\" alt=\"Development\" data-canonical-src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/-development-blue\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003eRecommended\u003c/code\u003e If available.\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003estring\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eType of the tool utilized by the agent [15]\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003efunction\u003c/code\u003e; \u003ccode\u003eextension\u003c/code\u003e; \u003ccode\u003edatastore\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/v1.44.0/docs/registry/attributes/process.md\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003eprocess.executable.path\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/c644474c011b0eb9c315c4bdb986289a81c148647d0db63e335e7cab68d0b4c5/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f2d72632d6d656469756d6f7263686964\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/c644474c011b0eb9c315c4bdb986289a81c148647d0db63e335e7cab68d0b4c5/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f2d72632d6d656469756d6f7263686964\" alt=\"Release Candidate\" data-canonical-src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/-rc-mediumorchid\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003eRecommended\u003c/code\u003e [16]\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003estring\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eThe full path to the process executable. On Linux based systems, can be set to the target of \u003ccode\u003eproc/[pid]/exe\u003c/code\u003e. On Windows, can be set to the result of \u003ccode\u003eGetProcessImageFileNameW\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003e/usr/bin/cmd/otelcol\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca href=\"/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions-genai/blob/main/docs/registry/attributes/gen-ai.md\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003egen_ai.tool.call.arguments\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/51c52913babf0af7e3699435eb2fa53f65cf91d89c23a9e0edba0fdd9de155d0/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f2d646576656c6f706d656e742d626c7565\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/51c52913babf0af7e3699435eb2fa53f65cf91d89c23a9e0edba0fdd9de155d0/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f2d646576656c6f706d656e742d626c7565\" alt=\"Development\" data-canonical-src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/-development-blue\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003eOpt-In\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eany\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eParameters passed to the tool call. [17]\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e{\u003cbr\u003e    \"location\": \"San Francisco?\",\u003cbr\u003e    \"date\": \"2025-10-01\"\u003cbr\u003e}\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca href=\"/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions-genai/blob/main/docs/registry/attributes/gen-ai.md\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003egen_ai.tool.call.result\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ca target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/51c52913babf0af7e3699435eb2fa53f65cf91d89c23a9e0edba0fdd9de155d0/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f2d646576656c6f706d656e742d626c7565\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/51c52913babf0af7e3699435eb2fa53f65cf91d89c23a9e0edba0fdd9de155d0/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f2d646576656c6f706d656e742d626c7565\" alt=\"Development\" data-canonical-src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/-development-blue\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003eOpt-In\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eany\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eThe result returned by the tool call (if any and if execution was successful). [18]\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e{\u003cbr\u003e  \"temperature_range\": {\u003cbr\u003e    \"high\": 75,\u003cbr\u003e    \"low\": 60\u003cbr\u003e  },\u003cbr\u003e  \"conditions\": \"sunny\"\u003cbr\u003e}\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/markdown-accessiblity-table\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e[1] \u003ccode\u003egen_ai.operation.name\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/strong\u003e If one of the predefined values applies, but specific system uses a different name it's RECOMMENDED to document it in the semantic conventions for specific GenAI system and use system-specific name in the instrumentation. If a different name is not documented, instrumentation libraries SHOULD use applicable predefined value.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e[2] \u003ccode\u003eerror.type\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/strong\u003e The \u003ccode\u003eerror.type\u003c/code\u003e SHOULD match the error code returned by the Generative AI provider or the client library,\nthe canonical name of exception that occurred, or another low-cardinality error identifier.\nInstrumentations SHOULD document the list of errors they report.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e[3] \u003ccode\u003egen_ai.conversation.id\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/strong\u003e Instrumentations SHOULD populate conversation id when they have an identifier\nfor the conversation readily available for a given operation, for example:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ewhen the client framework being instrumented manages conversation history\n(see \u003ca href=\"https://docs.llamaindex.ai/en/stable/module_guides/storing/chat_stores/\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003eLlamaIndex chat store\u003c/a\u003e,\n\u003ca href=\"https://reference.langchain.com/python/langchain-core/runnables/history/RunnableWithMessageHistory\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003eLangChain \u003ccode\u003esession_id\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/a\u003e,\nand \u003ca href=\"https://adk.dev/sessions/session\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003eGoogle ADK sessions\u003c/a\u003e)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ewhen instrumenting GenAI client libraries that maintain a conversation on the backend\n(see \u003ca href=\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/agents-session-state.html\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003eAWS Bedrock agent sessions\u003c/a\u003e,\n\u003ca href=\"https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/threads\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003eOpenAI Assistant threads\u003c/a\u003e)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eWhen no identifier for the conversation is available, instrumentations SHOULD NOT\npopulate conversation id. For example, a new UUID, a trace identifier, or a hash\nof request content SHOULD NOT be used as a fallback value.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eApplication developers that manage conversation history MAY add conversation id to GenAI and other\nspans or logs using custom span or log record processors or hooks provided by instrumentation\nlibraries.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e[4] \u003ccode\u003egen_ai.skill.name\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/strong\u003e If the command is associated with a skill and its name is available.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e[5] \u003ccode\u003egen_ai.skill.resource.name\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/strong\u003e If the command executes a named skill resource and the name is available.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e[6] \u003ccode\u003egen_ai.tool.call.id\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/strong\u003e If and only if the model or provider supplied a tool call identifier.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e[7] \u003ccode\u003egen_ai.tool.call.id\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/strong\u003e This attribute SHOULD be set to the identifier received from the model or provider\nif and only if one was supplied.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e[8] \u003ccode\u003eprocess.executable.name\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/strong\u003e If the tool directly executes a single process and the executable name is available.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e[9] \u003ccode\u003eprocess.exit.code\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/strong\u003e If the tool reports a single command or process exit code.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e[10] \u003ccode\u003egen_ai.skill.description\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/strong\u003e If the command is associated with a skill and its description is available.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e[11] \u003ccode\u003egen_ai.skill.description\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-alert markdown-alert-warning\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cp class=\"markdown-alert-title\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-alert mr-2\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"M6.457 1.047c.659-1.234 2.427-1.234 3.086 0l6.082 11.378A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 14.082 15H1.918a1.75 1.75 0 0 1-1.543-2.575Zm1.763.707a.25.25 0 0 0-.44 0L1.698 13.132a.25.25 0 0 0 .22.368h12.164a.25.25 0 0 0 .22-.368Zm.53 3.996v2.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.5 0v-2.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0ZM9 11a1 1 0 1 1-2 0 1 1 0 0 1 2 0Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003eWarning\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThis attribute may contain sensitive information.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e[12] \u003ccode\u003egen_ai.skill.source.uri\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/strong\u003e If the command is associated with a skill and its source URI is available.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e[13] \u003ccode\u003egen_ai.skill.source.uri\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/strong\u003e This SHOULD identify the skill source, not a temporary location where the\nskill was materialized for execution.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-alert markdown-alert-warning\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cp class=\"markdown-alert-title\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-alert mr-2\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"M6.457 1.047c.659-1.234 2.427-1.234 3.086 0l6.082 11.378A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 14.082 15H1.918a1.75 1.75 0 0 1-1.543-2.575Zm1.763.707a.25.25 0 0 0-.44 0L1.698 13.132a.25.25 0 0 0 .22.368h12.164a.25.25 0 0 0 .22-.368Zm.53 3.996v2.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.5 0v-2.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0ZM9 11a1 1 0 1 1-2 0 1 1 0 0 1 2 0Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003eWarning\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThis attribute may contain sensitive information.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eSensitive URI components, such as user information and access tokens in query\nparameters, SHOULD be scrubbed when instrumentations can identify them.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e[14] \u003ccode\u003egen_ai.tool.description\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-alert markdown-alert-warning\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cp class=\"markdown-alert-title\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-alert mr-2\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"M6.457 1.047c.659-1.234 2.427-1.234 3.086 0l6.082 11.378A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 14.082 15H1.918a1.75 1.75 0 0 1-1.543-2.575Zm1.763.707a.25.25 0 0 0-.44 0L1.698 13.132a.25.25 0 0 0 .22.368h12.164a.25.25 0 0 0 .22-.368Zm.53 3.996v2.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.5 0v-2.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0ZM9 11a1 1 0 1 1-2 0 1 1 0 0 1 2 0Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003eWarning\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThis attribute may contain sensitive information.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e[15] \u003ccode\u003egen_ai.tool.type\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/strong\u003e Extension: A tool executed on the agent-side to directly call external APIs, bridging the gap between the agent and real-world systems.\nAgent-side operations involve actions that are performed by the agent on the server or within the agent's controlled environment.\nFunction: A tool executed on the client-side, where the agent generates parameters for a predefined function, and the client executes the logic.\nClient-side operations are actions taken on the user's end or within the client application.\nDatastore: A tool used by the agent to access and query structured or unstructured external data for retrieval-augmented tasks or knowledge updates.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e[16] \u003ccode\u003eprocess.executable.path\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/strong\u003e If the tool directly executes a single process and the executable path is available.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e[17] \u003ccode\u003egen_ai.tool.call.arguments\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-alert markdown-alert-warning\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cp class=\"markdown-alert-title\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-alert mr-2\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"M6.457 1.047c.659-1.234 2.427-1.234 3.086 0l6.082 11.378A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 14.082 15H1.918a1.75 1.75 0 0 1-1.543-2.575Zm1.763.707a.25.25 0 0 0-.44 0L1.698 13.132a.25.25 0 0 0 .22.368h12.164a.25.25 0 0 0 .22-.368Zm.53 3.996v2.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.5 0v-2.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0ZM9 11a1 1 0 1 1-2 0 1 1 0 0 1 2 0Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003eWarning\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThis attribute may contain sensitive information.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eIt's expected to be an object - in case a serialized string is available\nto the instrumentation, the instrumentation SHOULD do the best effort to\ndeserialize it to an object.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eInstrumentations MUST follow \u003ca href=\"/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions-genai/blob/main/model/gen-ai/gen-ai-tool-call-arguments.json\"\u003eJSON schema\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eWhen the attribute is recorded on events, it MUST be recorded in structured form. When recorded on spans, it MAY be recorded as a JSON string if structured format is not supported and SHOULD be recorded in structured form otherwise.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e[18] \u003ccode\u003egen_ai.tool.call.result\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"markdown-alert markdown-alert-warning\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003cp class=\"markdown-alert-title\" dir=\"auto\"\u003e\u003csvg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-alert mr-2\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"M6.457 1.047c.659-1.234 2.427-1.234 3.086 0l6.082 11.378A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 14.082 15H1.918a1.75 1.75 0 0 1-1.543-2.575Zm1.763.707a.25.25 0 0 0-.44 0L1.698 13.132a.25.25 0 0 0 .22.368h12.164a.25.25 0 0 0 .22-.368Zm.53 3.996v2.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.5 0v-2.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0ZM9 11a1 1 0 1 1-2 0 1 1 0 0 1 2 0Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003eWarning\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThis attribute may contain sensitive information.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eIt's expected to be an object - in case a serialized string is available\nto the instrumentation, the instrumentation SHOULD do the best effort to\ndeserialize it to an object.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eInstrumentations MUST follow \u003ca href=\"/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions-genai/blob/main/model/gen-ai/gen-ai-tool-call-result.json\"\u003eJSON schema\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eWhen the attribute is recorded on events, it MUST be recorded in structured form. When recorded on spans, it MAY be recorded as a JSON string if structured format is not supported and SHOULD be recorded in structured form otherwise.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eThe following attributes can be important for 