<p dir="auto">Instrumentations MUST follow <a href="/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions-genai/blob/main/model/gen-ai/gen-ai-input-messages.json">JSON schema</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">When the attribute is recorded on events, it MUST be recorded in structured form. When recorded on spans, it MAY be recorded as a JSON string if structured format is not supported and SHOULD be recorded in structured form otherwise.</p>
<p dir="auto"><strong>[30] <code>gen_ai.output.messages</code>:</strong> Each message represents a single output choice/candidate generated by
the model. Each message corresponds to exactly one generation
(choice/candidate) and vice versa - one choice cannot be split across
multiple messages or one message cannot contain parts from multiple choices.</p>
<p dir="auto">Instrumentations MAY provide a way for users to filter or truncate
output messages. <code>gen_ai.response.finish_reasons</code> remains aligned with the
generations returned by the provider, not with a filtered or truncated
<code>gen_ai.output.messages</code> value.</p>
<p dir="auto">When an operation ends in an error, this attribute SHOULD only be set
when the operation produced output, including partial streamed output.
