<p dir="auto"><strong>Status:</strong> <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/51c52913babf0af7e3699435eb2fa53f65cf91d89c23a9e0edba0fdd9de155d0/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f2d646576656c6f706d656e742d626c7565"><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/51c52913babf0af7e3699435eb2fa53f65cf91d89c23a9e0edba0fdd9de155d0/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f2d646576656c6f706d656e742d626c7565" alt="Development" data-canonical-src="https://img.shields.io/badge/-development-blue" style="max-width: 100%;"></a></p>
<p dir="auto">Describes a tool call that executes one or more commands.</p>
<p dir="auto">This refinement applies when a tool represents command execution,
including the execution of skill's script.</p>
<p dir="auto">Examples include:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a href="https://openai.github.io/openai-agents-python/sandbox/guide/" rel="nofollow">OpenAI Agents</a>
<code>exec_command</code>, which runs both general commands and scripts from
materialized skills;</li>
<li><a href="https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/deepagents/overview" rel="nofollow">LangChain Deep Agents</a>
sandbox <code>execute</code>, which runs both general commands and skill scripts;</li>
<li><a href="https://strandsagents.com/docs/user-guide/sdk/plugins/skills/" rel="nofollow">Strands Agents</a>
<code>shell</code>, which is used for both general commands and bundled skill
scripts;</li>
<li><a href="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/bash-tool" rel="nofollow">Anthropic</a>
client <code>bash</code> for general commands;</li>
<li><a href="https://adk.dev/skills/" rel="nofollow">Google ADK</a> <code>run_skill_script</code>, which is
dedicated to scripts bundled with skills;</li>
<li><a href="https://docs.agno.com/skills/overview" rel="nofollow">Agno</a> <code>get_skill_script</code> when
called with <code>execute=true</code>.</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">Instrumentations MAY also emit additional spans following the
<a href="https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/semconv/cli/cli-spans/" rel="nofollow">CLI client span conventions</a>
for each observed command, script, or process execution.</p>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Span name</strong> SHOULD be:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><code>execute_tool {gen_ai.tool.name} {gen_ai.skill.name} {gen_ai.skill.resource.name}</code>
when the skill and resource names are both available;</li>
<li><code>execute_tool {gen_ai.tool.name} {gen_ai.skill.resource.name}</code> when only the
skill resource name is available;</li>
<li><code>execute_tool {gen_ai.tool.name} {process.executable.name}</code> when only the
executable name is available;</li>
<li><code>execute_tool {gen_ai.tool.name}</code> otherwise.</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">The skill name SHOULD NOT be appended without the resource name.</p>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Span kind</strong> SHOULD be <code>INTERNAL</code>.</p>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Span status</strong> SHOULD follow the <a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/v1.44.0/docs/general/recording-errors.md">Recording Errors</a> document.</p>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Requirement level:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/v1.44.0/docs/general/signal-requirement-level.md">Recommended</a>.</p>
